(B) PRE-EXISTING DETERMINISTIC COMPILER CRASH (blocked the full-app iOS+macOS
    build) — found, root-caused, and worked around with a 1-line behaviour-
    preserving change. FULL DISCLOSURE (Covenant 9 "no silent drift"):

    Symptom: `xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync … build test` aborted with
      swift-frontend SIGABRT (exit 134), llvm::report_fatal_error →
      report_at_maximum_capacity → SmallVector<unsigned int>::grow_pod, while:
        "4. While evaluating request IRGenRequest(IR Generation for file
            …/feature-views/AppearanceSettings.Controls.swift)
         5. While emitting IR SIL function @$sSbScA_pSgIeAghyg_SbIeAghn_TR"
      i.e. IRGen of a reabstraction thunk for an actor-isolated
      `(Bool) -> Void` closure. `report_at_maximum_capacity` is a SmallVector
      SIZE-OVERFLOW assertion (a bogus ~SIZE_MAX element request) — DETERMINISTIC,
      memory-independent. (A true OOM yields SIGKILL/bad_alloc, not this assert.)

    Proof of determinism (not host-contention OOM, despite the noisy host):
      • Crashed the SAME file + SAME thunk across 3 build configs
        (-jobs 20 batch, -jobs 4 batch, -jobs 4 single-file). A random OOM would
        strike different files each run; this never did.
      • Reproduced STANDALONE by replaying the isolated swift-frontend
        `-primary-file AppearanceSettings.Controls.swift` invocation → exit 134,
        "report_at_maximum_capacity", same thunk. RUN1_EXIT=134.
      • The file is 201 lines of idiomatic SwiftUI — nothing pathological.
      • It was committed TODAY (0dd623aa3, "add AppearanceSettings surface (P4)"),
        i.e. AFTER the last green run — so this is a PRE-EXISTING P4 defect, NOT
        introduced by this P9-0001 change set (I never touched it otherwise).

    Trigger + fix (AppearanceSettings.Controls.swift, AppearanceToggleRow.body):
        - Toggle("", isOn: Binding(get: { isOn }, set: onChange))      // crashes
        + Toggle("", isOn: Binding(get: { isOn }, set: { onChange($0) }))
      `onChange` is `@MainActor (Bool) -> Void`; passing it DIRECTLY as
      `Binding.set` makes IRGen emit the buggy actor-isolated reabstraction thunk.
      Wrapping it in a trivial forwarding closure sidesteps the thunk. Behaviour
      is IDENTICAL (same call, same MainActor context); the public API of
      AppearanceToggleRow is unchanged (no caller edits). Validated via the
      standalone reproducer: REPRO2_EXIT=0, 0 crashes, 0 type errors; then via the
      full green build below. This is the ONLY non-placeholder source change, and
      the ONLY file with the crash (all 2,391 other primary files compiled).

